# Optional dependencies are omitted, and both `npm install` here and `npm ci` in CI
# see the same tree because of it.
#
# The problem this solves: `rpc-websockets` (reached through `@solana/web3.js`)
# declares `bufferutil` and `utf-8-validate` as optional. They are native addons, npm
# skips them silently on this machine, and the lockfile is written without them — so
# `npm ci` on Linux, where they *would* build, refuses with "Missing: bufferutil from
# lock file". A lockfile generated on one platform is simply not complete for another
# when optional native addons are involved.
#
# Omitting them costs nothing here. They are performance addons for `ws`, which this
# app never uses at runtime — React Native and the browser supply their own WebSocket,
# and `ws` is reached only by Node-side tooling.
omit=optional
